    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0210" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1140/253: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-24T14:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 24, 1918—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 24—10:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. Secret for the President. In your announcement quoted in your telegram
                    number 16<anchor n="19" xml:id="d108-f1"/> you state, “The President will sail
                    for France.” I understand this to mean that you will go direct from the United
                    States to France and not pass through England. Please confirm this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
